   "category": "Multi-agent",
   "status": "built",
   "llm": true,
   "writes": true,
   "summary": "A Parser and a Reasoner on a self-hosted Qwen3-4B model, where the Reasoner uses NextNode's graph tools, and a Reviewer from a different model family (Llama 3.1) that verifies the curriculum against the graph. Runs as a fixed script on small models, or under an Omnigent orchestrator on stronger ones.",
   "how": [
    "scripts/curriculum_run.py runs the steps in a fixed order: parse resume and job, reason with the graph tools, review with read-only tools, at most one revision. Prompts, models and tool allow-lists come from the Omnigent bundle.",
    "Guardrails in code: each agent only gets its allow-listed tools, the reviewer never gets a write tool, tool calls are capped.",
    "The verdict comes from the reviewer's seven checks done in code against the graph (fit score, roadmap coverage, prerequisite order, builds_on owned, copied priority and reason, no URLs, hours). The Llama 3.1 reviewer's findings are kept as advisory notes: on the first local run it reported a failure for all seven checks on a curriculum the graph confirmed correct.",
    "The Omnigent orchestrator (omnigent/nextnode_curriculum, v0.19.1) is kept for stronger models: on Qwen3-4B it stalled after dispatching the parsers, which is why the scripted runner exists.",
    "No Gemini calls: the agents reach vLLM (or the Ollama stand-in) on localhost:8000/v1."
   ],
