   "llm": false,
   "writes": false,
   "summary": "Kubernetes manifests, an AWS EKS cluster config and scripts that run an open-weight model (Qwen3-4B) on one cloud GPU behind vLLM's OpenAI-compatible API, so the agents have no rate limit. A $0 local rehearsal tests everything except the GPU first. GPU quota approved; not yet deployed.",
   "how": [
    "scripts/aws_gpu.ps1 up creates an EKS cluster with one g6.xlarge (NVIDIA L4) and no NAT gateway, or resumes it; pause scales the GPU node to 0; down deletes everything. status prints the current hourly cost.",
    "kubectl apply -k deploy/k8s/vllm: one GPU pod, cluster-internal service only, model cache on an encrypted gp3 volume, tool calling on (hermes parser).",
    "scripts/vllm_tunnel.ps1 -Deploy creates a random API key Secret, waits for the model, then opens a loopback-only port-forward to localhost:8000/v1.",
    "Roughly $0.90/hour while running; tests check the manifests, the cluster config and that the pod fits the node.",
    "Before AWS: vllm_tunnel.ps1 -Deploy -Local runs the same manifests on Docker Desktop Kubernetes (vLLM CPU image, a 0.6B model); vllm_standin.ps1 serves the real Qwen3-4B on Ollama at the same address so the agents run unchanged.",
    "scripts/vllm_smoke.py checks any of them: API key enforced, model name, chat, structured tool calls, and (--mcp) the model calling the real MCP tools until it reports the graph's fit score."
   ],
